Shiori for Classic Macintosh
Version @VERSION@

Search your pages in Hister and your notes in Kura from a Mac Plus or later, on System 6.0.8 or System 7.

What you need
- MacTCP 2.0.6 or later, on Ethernet.
- The bridge (mac-bridge) running on your network, next to Hister.
- A room token for this Mac, from the sign-in helper's sessions page.

Installing
- Shiori: copy it anywhere.
- Shiori Search, the desk accessory: on System 6, install it with Font/DA Mover. On System 7, open it and drag Shiori Search to the System Folder.

First run
Preferences opens: enter the bridge's two addresses (http://<IP address>:<port>/) and the room token. They stay on this Mac, in Shiori Preferences. Keep that file off shared disks: the token is in it.

